Carry a platform drag over Wayland

gpui's Wayland backend binds wl_data_device for the clipboard and for
drags of files alone. Carry a drag the application offers over on a
wl_data_source with an icon surface of its own, and report a drag
carrying the mime type the application takes to whichever window it is
carried over.

A wl_data_source reports a release over a surface that takes nothing
exactly as it reports a gesture called off, so the source alone cannot
say whether a panel was let go of over the desktop or the gesture
abandoned. Mutter reports the release of a source carrying an
xdg_toplevel_drag_v1 as a drop and only then cancels the source, which
this patch reads as PlatformDragEnd::Released. Neither
xdg-toplevel-drag-v1 nor wl_data_source promises that ordering: it is
Mutter's treatment of the object, observed on GNOME 50.4 and on no other
compositor.

xdg-toplevel-drag-v1 is a staging protocol and adoption is uneven; the
compositors built on wlroots (Sway, Hyprland, river, cage) and Weston
offer no xdg_toplevel_drag_manager_v1 at all. The patch asks for the
object only where the compositor advertises the global, so on such a
session a release over the desktop reaches the application as
PlatformDragEnd::Cancelled and tearing a panel out of its window does
nothing.

